# WayExpand evdev capture backend (--source=evdev) reads keyboard-capable
# /dev/input/event* nodes directly. Most systemd-based distributions already
# grant GROUP="input" MODE="0660" to input devices via their own default rules
# (see /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/50-udev-default.rules); this file only reasserts
# that same default explicitly for udev's keyboard-class event nodes, so
# WayExpand does not silently depend on it being present. It does not grant
# anything beyond what a standard systemd installation already grants members
# of the `input` group.
#
# This is the current legacy/simple permission model. It is installed by
# scripts/install-evdev-permissions.sh, which also adds the
# invoking user to the `input` group. Read SECURITY.md for what that
# membership grants before enabling --source=evdev: it may let a process read
# raw input event devices beyond WayExpand's matcher, depending on the rest of
# the distribution's input group policy. See docs/EVDEV_ACCESS_DESIGN.md for
# the active-seat ACL and device-broker investigation.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="?*", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"
